    {
      "id": "grammar-simple-future",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "infinitivo + terminación de futuro",
      "questionEn": "How do you say what someone will do in Spanish?",
      "answerEn": "Keep the action verb in its dictionary form and add a future ending such as -é, -ás, -á, -emos, -éis, or -án.",
      "noteEn": "The dictionary form is the unchanged form ending in -ar, -er, or -ir. The ending identifies the person: sentir plus -á gives sentirá, and ver plus -á gives verá. A few common verbs change their stem, but use the same endings.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Marta llamará mañana.",
        "en": "Marta will call tomorrow."
      },
      "tags": [
